182
00:14:36,957 --> 00:14:42,339
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're not denying it, but you're certainly not forgetting which... where you are on account of it.

183
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:55,625
[SPEAKER_00]: And, I mean, a good point as well is that it's... it's important to realize that you can

184
00:14:56,781 --> 00:15:20,813
[SPEAKER_00]: If you are, like, afraid of having such thoughts, or even, you know, seeing yourself having such thoughts, you don't want to kind of admit them to yourself or something, you don't want to be having those thoughts, that in itself will make it hard to actually correctly attend them, because you will be, like, trying to... by trying to ignore them,

185
00:15:21,567 --> 00:15:24,769
[SPEAKER_00]: That's already a wrong way of attending them.

186
00:15:24,889 --> 00:15:27,270
[SPEAKER_00]: You're giving them that wrong attention.

187
00:15:27,690 --> 00:15:31,672
[SPEAKER_00]: And actually, that's allowing them to proliferate there in the background, just ignoring them.

188
00:15:31,692 --> 00:15:33,774
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's really the root of all unwholesome.

189
00:15:33,814 --> 00:15:41,077
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the presence of those images, in regard to sensuality, or images in regard to your will, or in regard to worry, that's not the root of unwholesome.

190
00:15:41,197 --> 00:15:42,338
[SPEAKER_01]: That's not the root of suffering.

191
00:15:43,379 --> 00:15:48,981
[SPEAKER_01]: That's in those numerous suttas in the Guttara Nikaya, where the Buddha said, there is not a single thing such as

192
00:15:50,757 --> 00:15:59,801
[SPEAKER_01]: ayoniso manasikāra, the incoherent intention, that makes unwholesome things increase, wholesome decrease, and unreasonably unwholesome to arise.

193
00:16:01,122 --> 00:16:09,206
[SPEAKER_01]: And consequently, there's not a single thing that makes unwholesome things decrease and wholesome increase, such as yoniso manasikāra.

194
00:16:09,246 --> 00:16:10,586
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that is the root of it.

195
00:16:11,827 --> 00:16:15,648
[SPEAKER_01]: And, eh... and that's exactly how one becomes established in virtue.

196
00:16:15,989 --> 00:16:18,710
[SPEAKER_01]: You realize, by practicing the same,

197
00:16:20,953 --> 00:16:26,375
[SPEAKER_01]: Restraint in regard to the body, the speech, and the mind on the right mental level.

198
00:16:26,435 --> 00:16:30,297
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, okay, so restraint on the mind is not just denial of things.

199
00:16:31,057 --> 00:16:35,939
[SPEAKER_01]: I just deny things to arise, to not arise, because you realize, well, that's not even the restraint on the level of the body.

200
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:44,183
[SPEAKER_01]: The restraint on the level of the body is not acting out towards possibilities that remain there in the world, but you choose to abstain from it.

201
00:16:45,065 --> 00:16:51,691
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, your abstaining, your sensory strength, exists concurrently with those possibilities.

202
00:16:52,612 --> 00:16:54,374
[SPEAKER_01]: Neither are excluded.

203
00:16:54,394 --> 00:16:57,757
[SPEAKER_01]: You just choose to maintain this, in regard to that, that is still present.

204
00:16:57,997 --> 00:17:00,059
[SPEAKER_01]: Very much so.

205
00:17:00,079 --> 00:17:07,687
[SPEAKER_01]: Same with speech, and then you recognize, oh, so it's exactly the same principle with the mind, which is why, as I said, in the suttas, the whole thing is often bundled together.

206
00:17:08,558 --> 00:17:09,639
[SPEAKER_01]: The same purification.

207
00:17:09,699 --> 00:17:12,562
[SPEAKER_01]: It does not change or skip a beat and become something else.

208
00:17:13,202 --> 00:17:15,505
[SPEAKER_01]: It's exactly the same development all the way through.

209
00:17:16,566 --> 00:17:19,068
[SPEAKER_01]: But yes, that mental level needs to be discerned, of course.

210
00:17:19,869 --> 00:17:24,493
[SPEAKER_01]: So, recognizing images associated with centrality, images associated with

211
00:17:24,985 --> 00:17:26,766
[SPEAKER_01]: With your will, with any hindrance.

212
00:17:27,426 --> 00:17:29,766
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's like, okay, so I don't try to get rid of them.

213
00:17:30,107 --> 00:17:40,150
[SPEAKER_01]: I know that they're there, but I do not allow them to become, as I said, the center of my focus, either through trying to get rid of them, fear them, act out of them, and so on.

214
00:17:41,350 --> 00:17:50,693
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the whole mindfulness of the body that gets developed, eh... because that's what's always concurrently present with... regardless of what state of mind you're in.

215
00:17:52,713 --> 00:17:55,322
[SPEAKER_01]: You have your body there enduring simultaneously to that extent.

216
00:17:56,406 --> 00:17:57,852
[SPEAKER_01]: And that doesn't change, cannot change.

217
00:17:58,713 --> 00:18:02,056
[SPEAKER_00]: Being fully aware of them is not awareness.

218
00:18:03,016 --> 00:18:03,737
[SPEAKER_00]: It's absorption.

219
00:18:03,757 --> 00:18:10,442
[SPEAKER_00]: You can be fully absorbed in them, but then you're not aware of yourself or anything else in your experience.

220
00:18:11,023 --> 00:18:20,410
[SPEAKER_00]: Or, you can be, like, half aware of something there, but trying to kind of ignore it and pretend it's not there, and, like, focus on the leaves and everything else that you're doing.

221
00:18:21,031 --> 00:18:25,254
[SPEAKER_00]: And, equally, you're not... you're not actually properly aware of the thing.

222
00:18:25,294 --> 00:18:26,255
[SPEAKER_00]: You're trying to ignore it.

223
00:18:26,315 --> 00:18:26,675
[SPEAKER_00]: Whereas,

224
00:18:28,777 --> 00:18:37,628
[SPEAKER_00]: Because these things can really only operate where there's kind of a degree of ignorance, a degree of, like, ignoring it, ignoring one end of your experience at the expense of the other.

225
00:18:38,529 --> 00:18:44,056
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I mean, I'm just saying that because, like, the concurrency and so on can sound a bit...

226
00:18:44,236 --> 00:18:44,757
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the thing.

227
00:18:44,777 --> 00:18:45,458
[SPEAKER_00]: It's that deliberation.

228
00:18:45,478 --> 00:18:45,618
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

229
00:18:45,638 --> 00:18:46,959
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it boils down...

230
00:19:02,538 --> 00:19:04,940
[SPEAKER_01]: To the very deliberation aspect of it.

231
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:12,705
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's just that, obviously, you need to first restrain other, more coarser forms of deliberation.

232
00:19:12,765 --> 00:19:20,991
[SPEAKER_01]: But, once you start to recognize that allowing those images to take the center stage of your experience, it's an act, it's a deliberate act.

233
00:19:21,531 --> 00:19:23,973
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's like, oh, I need to restrain that.

234
00:19:25,951 --> 00:19:26,972
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, I agree.

235
00:19:27,012 --> 00:19:45,288
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, whether we talk about intention or concurrency, all of these are kind of an indirect ways of pointing at there is an act of deliberation, either towards I want to get rid of these thoughts, again, it's a deliberate kind of denial, or I'll deliberately give in to them.

236
00:19:45,328 --> 00:19:46,789
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll just... they're pressuring me.

237
00:19:46,849 --> 00:19:53,715
[SPEAKER_01]: These images are just taking up all of my attention span, and there is always a point where you choose to give in to that.

238
00:19:54,281 --> 00:19:56,503
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, oh, that's what you need to not do.

239
00:19:56,543 --> 00:19:59,265
[SPEAKER_01]: So, just don't give in to that last drop.

240
00:19:59,965 --> 00:20:04,428
[SPEAKER_01]: You can have all those images all you want, but if you don't allow that last...

241
00:20:04,688 --> 00:20:07,810
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, I will allow them to take the center stage.

242
00:20:08,911 --> 00:20:09,592
[SPEAKER_01]: You are in the clear.

243
00:20:10,472 --> 00:20:11,053
[SPEAKER_01]: You are in the clear.

244
00:20:11,133 --> 00:20:18,378
[SPEAKER_01]: And if you sustain that last not giving in on that mental level, the establishment of virtue, in virtue, is taking place.

245
00:20:19,951 --> 00:20:21,572
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, exactly, that comes down to that.

246
00:20:22,013 --> 00:20:25,275
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, so yes, you are actually addressing things in the root.

247
00:20:25,415 --> 00:20:39,587
[SPEAKER_01]: So then, the future bodily misbehavior or verbal misbehavior will be even less likely, if already on that mental level, you're recognizing that deliberate act of allowing these things, giving in, and you're not doing it.

248
00:20:40,748 --> 00:20:41,228
[SPEAKER_01]: Just that.

249
00:20:41,629 --> 00:20:44,751
[SPEAKER_01]: You let them be, but you don't do just that last last drop.

250
00:20:44,791 --> 00:20:46,953
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly what the suttas would be describing.

251
00:20:46,993 --> 00:20:49,215
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, he doesn't welcome these thoughts.

252
00:20:49,972 --> 00:20:51,554
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you realize, they're there.

253
00:20:51,834 --> 00:20:53,236
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not a question of getting rid of them.

254
00:20:53,296 --> 00:20:55,138
[SPEAKER_01]: The question is of not welcoming them.

255
00:20:55,899 --> 00:21:03,347
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you have even thoughts of ill will, that are unpleasant, you do welcome them, to then try to resolve it or act out and so on.

256
00:21:03,547 --> 00:21:07,872
[SPEAKER_01]: And there is that... it feels that it's almost like, eh...

257
00:21:09,757 --> 00:21:18,419
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not subconscious, but it kind of feels like an unconscious habit of... you just can't help but welcome first, and then try to resolve it.

258
00:21:18,939 --> 00:21:30,981
[SPEAKER_01]: And the reason why you can't help but welcome first, mentally, is because physically you still have not been thoroughly developed in that uprooting those wrong types of deliberate acts, nor verbally.

259
00:21:31,461 --> 00:21:37,882
[SPEAKER_01]: You have not allowed those things to come up closer to the mental level, whereby the mental deliberation would become more obvious.

260
00:21:40,192 --> 00:21:59,457
[SPEAKER_01]: And you do always see that, as I said, like, you can be dwelling physically restrained, but then, something that's not necessarily unwholesome, like, and you kind of know that in and of itself, and nobody will be upset, but you know that it's rooted in desire.

261
00:22:00,377 --> 00:22:03,198
[SPEAKER_01]: Or you know that in you, oh, this is rooted in ill-will.

262
00:22:04,553 --> 00:22:11,395
[SPEAKER_01]: But it is not a technical prohibition against saying something, but, again, you know that you are doing it out of your will.

263
00:22:12,816 --> 00:22:16,157
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you deliberately, then, choose to act out of that.

264
00:22:16,837 --> 00:22:26,360
[SPEAKER_01]: You deliberately choose to ignore the fact that, yeah, I know it's technically nothing wrong, but I'm not here to deal with technicalities, I'm here to uproot suffering and free myself from craving.

265
00:22:26,860 --> 00:22:29,981
[SPEAKER_01]: And then you realize also, then, there is no excuse, there is no exception.

266
00:22:30,722 --> 00:22:34,343
[SPEAKER_01]: If things are rooted in obvious unwholesome states of mind, I should not say them.

267
00:22:35,215 --> 00:22:36,896
[SPEAKER_01]: It doesn't matter what happens to the world.

268
00:22:38,497 --> 00:22:47,741
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you've been practicing that long enough, you will get to recognize that even before it comes to, like, speech and pertaining to speech.

269
00:22:47,781 --> 00:22:55,985
[SPEAKER_01]: You will recognize those types of same deliberations and allowances and welcoming and accepting and turning a blind eye on that mental level.

270
00:23:06,892 --> 00:23:30,078
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's also, it relates to what you were saying about it being equivalent to the right, getting the right view, because it also relates to how the suttas describe it as becoming independent of others, in the sense of not being able to put any

271
00:23:31,597 --> 00:23:52,259
[SPEAKER_00]: The thing that others might say, or no matter how much the world sort of says that this is okay, no matter how many other people who are all, you know, I respect them and everything, and they all do it, so it must be fine, or whatever other kind of notion or relying on others to some extent, it can't, kind of,

272
00:23:54,446 --> 00:24:10,372
[SPEAKER_00]: Get prioritized above what you know your intention is rooted in, because you always know that you can't... you can deny it, you can cover it up with other things, but fundamentally, if you look, it's always... your intentions will tell you what they are.

273
00:24:10,892 --> 00:24:11,072
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

274
00:24:11,652 --> 00:24:14,733
[SPEAKER_00]: And that has to be... that just has to be discerned.

275
00:24:14,753 --> 00:24:19,795
[SPEAKER_01]: And also, then you could also see how getting the right view is not an accident.

276
00:24:21,496 --> 00:24:22,696
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not like a...

277
00:24:24,697 --> 00:24:28,299
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not a lucky kind of experience that somebody just stumbles upon.

278
00:24:28,339 --> 00:24:33,181
[SPEAKER_01]: No, it's just you go in this direction of development and established in virtue equals right view.

279
00:24:46,888 --> 00:24:51,831
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, you realize then a person could, out of faith, take on the precepts,

280
00:24:53,140 --> 00:24:55,041
[SPEAKER_01]: Learn about what's wholesome, what's unwholesome.

281
00:24:56,141 --> 00:24:58,482
[SPEAKER_01]: Abstain from unwholesome physically.

282
00:24:58,522 --> 00:25:10,667
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, when the mind, when the mentally, mind starts to pressure them, and they start, you know, they might not be acting out physically, but they want to act out verbally, or distract themselves verbally, and start engaging in all this, then they restrain that.

283
00:25:11,367 --> 00:25:13,288
[SPEAKER_01]: They recognize, okay, no, I will not give in to that.

284
00:25:14,108 --> 00:25:20,451
[SPEAKER_01]: Regardless of whether it's acceptable or not, I know that it's rooted in the same type of pressure that I'm restraining in regard to bodily behavior.

285
00:25:21,676 --> 00:25:29,161
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if they haven't been acting out of speech, then either... Again, it's like, obviously depends on individual, but it won't be before long.

286
00:25:29,201 --> 00:25:33,023
[SPEAKER_01]: If this is done rightly, you will get to then see the same pressure on the mental level.

287
00:25:34,004 --> 00:25:38,647
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yes, you're not acting by the body, you're not acting by the speech, but are you acting by the mind?

288
00:25:39,407 --> 00:25:40,048
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you acting out?

289
00:25:41,229 --> 00:25:47,793
[SPEAKER_01]: And as we described, acting out by the mind incurs a certain, that degree of

290
00:25:49,138 --> 00:25:51,199
[SPEAKER_01]: Losing self-awareness in regard to your own thoughts.

291
00:25:51,779 --> 00:25:55,500
[SPEAKER_01]: Choosing to deliberately allow them to take the center stage.

292
00:25:55,901 --> 00:25:59,902
[SPEAKER_01]: Not your self-awareness in regard to the thoughts, the concurrency of it, and so on.

293
00:26:00,642 --> 00:26:16,829
[SPEAKER_01]: But even, as I said, without going into the simultaneity and the principle behind, just as a mere practice, you're like, okay, so I will not deliberately allow my attention to rest upon thoughts of sensuality when they come up and start pressuring me.

294
00:26:17,029 --> 00:26:17,349
[SPEAKER_01]: Images.

295
00:26:18,905 --> 00:26:26,468
[SPEAKER_01]: I will not deliberately allow to rest my attention, myself, my experience as a whole, on the images of ill-will.

296
00:26:27,389 --> 00:26:30,750
[SPEAKER_01]: They can be there, but I won't get that.

297
00:26:31,010 --> 00:26:37,493
[SPEAKER_01]: I won't, like, take them and put them in front of me, whereby, you know, everything else is going to start revolving around them.

298
00:26:38,193 --> 00:26:40,354
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's how you don't act out of it.

299
00:26:40,934 --> 00:26:42,635
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, when there is a

300
00:26:43,793 --> 00:26:48,056
[SPEAKER_01]: A possibility to act out with your body in an unwholesome manner.

301
00:26:48,356 --> 00:26:55,441
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't go and destroy the tempting thing and kill people that might excite you or irritate you.

302
00:26:55,541 --> 00:26:56,602
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, I'll have to get rid of it.

303
00:26:56,662 --> 00:26:57,943
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how I free myself from the world.

304
00:26:58,343 --> 00:26:59,644
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you realize, oh, so you can't do...

305
00:27:00,224 --> 00:27:01,465
[SPEAKER_01]: The same applies to the mind.

306
00:27:01,525 --> 00:27:03,907
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't just, oh, I'll get rid of these thoughts.

307
00:27:04,227 --> 00:27:05,128
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll forget about them.

308
00:27:05,168 --> 00:27:06,169
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll focus on something else.

309
00:27:06,549 --> 00:27:07,830
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, well, yeah, but again,

310
00:27:08,450 --> 00:27:09,670
[SPEAKER_01]: The same principle remains.

311
00:27:09,731 --> 00:27:13,972
[SPEAKER_01]: You still... the root of the problem is not having those thoughts in the first place.

312
00:27:14,052 --> 00:27:18,714
[SPEAKER_01]: The root is that you cannot not allow them, deliberately, to take the center stage.

313
00:27:19,354 --> 00:27:20,314
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the training is there.

314
00:27:20,414 --> 00:27:20,714
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

315
00:27:21,235 --> 00:27:35,780
[SPEAKER_01]: When the thoughts are present, I must have to recognize that deliberate act of allowing them to to become sort of established in this center experience, and then everything I else... everything else I do becomes rooted in it.

316
00:27:37,402 --> 00:27:42,943
[SPEAKER_01]: So, abstaining from that last allowance, that last welcoming, which is, as I said, a deliberate act.

317
00:27:43,023 --> 00:27:50,605
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if it feels like automatic and subconscious, it's only because you haven't developed your behavior sufficiently in those more coarse manners.

318
00:27:53,525 --> 00:28:02,147
[SPEAKER_01]: Do you, through your act or through your reasoning, are you putting or implying the blame to be in those images or in you wrongly attending to them?

319
00:28:03,047 --> 00:28:04,148
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the key here.

320
00:28:05,569 --> 00:28:14,113
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, if you're denying it, if you're using meditation concentration technique, if you're doing this in response to that, that implication is always going to be there.

321
00:28:14,213 --> 00:28:21,477
[SPEAKER_01]: You think those images are the problem, and that's why you don't see the root of the problem, and that's why you won't be free in regard to it, and that's why you won't be established in virtue.

322
00:28:23,257 --> 00:28:25,398
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's you attending to them wrongly.

323
00:28:26,299 --> 00:28:30,561
[SPEAKER_01]: In other words, you letting them take the center stage is the wrong attention.

324
00:28:31,303 --> 00:28:36,609
[SPEAKER_01]: So, abstaining from that deliberate act, you are purifying way of attending to things, right?

325
00:28:39,031 --> 00:28:43,977
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not a separate mystical practice, or I gotta practice yoniso and then apply it.

326
00:28:44,097 --> 00:28:44,237
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

327
00:28:44,637 --> 00:28:51,685
[SPEAKER_01]: Not allowing them to take the center stage, which is a deliberate act, however subtle it might be, is your yoniso manasikāra practice.

328
00:28:52,540 --> 00:28:53,860
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not a question of focus, really.

329
00:28:53,880 --> 00:29:00,982
[SPEAKER_01]: The question is more of a deliberate degree of unfocus in regard to things you should be unfocused from.

330
00:29:01,063 --> 00:29:01,603
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, exactly.

331
00:29:02,403 --> 00:29:04,764
[SPEAKER_02]: Because the focus is... you're being pressured to focus.

332
00:29:04,844 --> 00:29:05,204
[SPEAKER_02]: Exactly.

333
00:29:05,224 --> 00:29:11,786
[SPEAKER_01]: You're being pressured to give in and welcome this and accept it and then deal with it, either through denial or indulgence.

334
00:29:11,906 --> 00:29:12,426
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter.

335
00:29:13,026 --> 00:29:15,967
[SPEAKER_01]: But first and foremost, it's like that pressure to take me.

336
00:29:16,846 --> 00:29:19,288
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, no, that's, that's the root of unwholesome.

337
00:29:19,348 --> 00:29:20,408
[SPEAKER_01]: Me, taking it.

338
00:29:20,909 --> 00:29:23,070
[SPEAKER_01]: Not this thing being there or pressuring me either.

339
00:29:24,151 --> 00:29:27,072
[SPEAKER_02]: And the breath is there regardless of whether you attend to it or not.

340
00:29:27,233 --> 00:29:29,314
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, everything is there regardless of whether you're attending or not.

341
00:29:29,434 --> 00:29:34,337
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, the five aggregates, the body, the four postures, the breath, whichever basis for your mindfulness you want to take.

342
00:29:35,658 --> 00:29:40,561
[SPEAKER_00]: That's also why it equals, like, well, sort of safety, sense of

343
00:29:41,082 --> 00:29:48,707
[SPEAKER_00]: Sense of safety, in terms of it being something that can only ever be... it's totally in your hand.

344
00:29:48,847 --> 00:29:54,091
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, nothing can... no amount of images that come up.

345
00:29:54,591 --> 00:30:03,157
[SPEAKER_00]: If your view, to some degree, implies that the problem is in those images, you can never feel safe, because it's always possible that some image can come up.

346
00:30:03,177 --> 00:30:04,638
[SPEAKER_01]: And you have absolutely nothing to bring those images up.

347
00:30:04,658 --> 00:30:05,598
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no way to hide from them.

348
00:30:05,638 --> 00:30:07,500
[SPEAKER_00]: No matter what you can do, it can still...

349
00:30:08,545 --> 00:30:14,117
[SPEAKER_00]: It still might be possible that this might arise and there's no way of knowing or being sure that this can never arise again.

350
00:30:14,317 --> 00:30:14,698
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

351
00:30:15,483 --> 00:30:28,270
[SPEAKER_00]: But, so, like, to the extent that you have some kind of notion, or fear, or way, what if this comes up, or what if that comes up, you can sort of know that your... your virtue is not completely established.

352
00:30:28,330 --> 00:30:36,094
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if it were, virtue that is... being established in virtue means recognizing virtue as something that no... nothing can...

353
00:30:36,574 --> 00:30:37,815
[SPEAKER_01]: It's coming between you and...

354
00:30:37,835 --> 00:30:38,755
[SPEAKER_01]: It's coming between you and it.

355
00:30:38,795 --> 00:30:39,316
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, exactly.

356
00:30:39,516 --> 00:30:41,077
[SPEAKER_00]: It is... it is always in your hand.

357
00:30:41,097 --> 00:30:41,857
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah.

358
00:30:42,956 --> 00:30:50,620
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just, as I said, for most people, it's too subtle, because they haven't been practicing sensory strain properly with the body, nor with the speech.

359
00:30:51,100 --> 00:30:53,741
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this feels like too subtle to notice.

360
00:30:54,302 --> 00:30:59,304
[SPEAKER_01]: And thus, when you say you should not welcome these thoughts, for people that equals, I must get rid of those thoughts.

361
00:30:59,604 --> 00:31:00,965
[SPEAKER_01]: But that's not the same statement.

362
00:31:01,515 --> 00:31:16,085
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you... if you look at your intentions on the level of body and the speech, and, as I said, not act out of them, and then endure the mental pressure and state in regard to it, this deliberate act of accepting images on that subtle level will become apparent.

363
00:31:16,865 --> 00:31:18,146
[SPEAKER_01]: Somebody said something upsetting.

364
00:31:18,627 --> 00:31:25,351
[SPEAKER_01]: There is a pressure, there is an influx of images that are associated with that person in a... like a manner of ill-will.

365
00:31:27,533 --> 00:31:30,255
[SPEAKER_01]: While I'm sitting here talking to you, I could choose now

366
00:31:31,067 --> 00:31:41,970
[SPEAKER_01]: To withdraw my attention from sitting and talking to you, and allow these thoughts to take the center stage, and start to revolve, and feed, and this and that, and I should have said, I will say next time...

367
00:31:42,700 --> 00:31:51,668
[SPEAKER_01]: Or, I was like, no, I'll let that domain, that entire domain of the mind that revolves around these images, I'll let it be there, but I will not allow it to deliberately take over me.

368
00:31:51,808 --> 00:31:52,128
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

369
00:31:52,609 --> 00:31:52,949
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

370
00:31:52,989 --> 00:31:53,930
[SPEAKER_01]: Just that last drop.

371
00:31:53,990 --> 00:31:55,431
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, oh, it's a restraint.

372
00:31:56,072 --> 00:32:01,036
[SPEAKER_01]: It's exact same principle of restraining the body, restraining the speech, I'm restraining the mind.

373
00:32:02,170 --> 00:32:07,052
[SPEAKER_01]: Restraining the mind means not allowing your mind to take over you, whereby you lose your self-awareness.

374
00:32:07,373 --> 00:32:12,895
[SPEAKER_01]: Does not mean denying my mind, denying these thoughts, trying to get rid of them, trying to counter them or something.

375
00:32:13,195 --> 00:32:15,897
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you don't do that in regard to things that tempt you by the body.

376
00:32:15,917 --> 00:32:17,437
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not countering them constantly.

377
00:32:18,258 --> 00:32:20,999
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, if you see something beautiful, you go and destroy it and make it ugly.

378
00:32:21,079 --> 00:32:21,239
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

379
00:32:22,140 --> 00:32:28,343
[SPEAKER_01]: So, restraining your mind means restraining, basically, the images when they present themselves from

380
00:32:29,210 --> 00:32:41,539
[SPEAKER_01]: Overwhelming you, in a sense of making you lose self-awareness and making you basically allow them, accept them as the center stage of your efforts and acts.

381
00:32:43,941 --> 00:32:50,346
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's where that whole kind of the necessity of purifying your bodily behavior first, it's not optional.

382
00:32:51,607 --> 00:32:53,388
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, if you're still giving in by the body,

383
00:32:55,005 --> 00:32:56,365
[SPEAKER_01]: All these things will remain abstract.

384
00:32:56,646 --> 00:32:57,866
[SPEAKER_01]: It would be too subtle to see.

385
00:32:58,186 --> 00:33:02,527
[SPEAKER_01]: Because even the bodily intention, of its course, nature, you still give in.

386
00:33:03,047 --> 00:33:08,769
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means you still imply, basically, that the problem is in things that tempted you.

387
00:33:08,809 --> 00:33:12,930
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why you give in to them, or you act out of them with anger, or whichever way.

388
00:33:14,351 --> 00:33:15,911
[SPEAKER_01]: And so that needs to be contained first.

389
00:33:17,792 --> 00:33:19,212
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, on the subtler level, speech.

390
00:33:19,472 --> 00:33:19,693
[SPEAKER_01]: Same.

391
00:33:20,433 --> 00:33:24,294
[SPEAKER_01]: Things you say, things you want to say, pressure to say, and so on.

392
00:33:25,900 --> 00:33:26,641
[SPEAKER_01]: Same recognition.

393
00:33:26,981 --> 00:33:28,122
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it rooted in the pressure?

394
00:33:29,283 --> 00:33:29,763
[SPEAKER_01]: I won't say.

395
00:33:29,963 --> 00:33:31,625
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll say everything else, if I have to.

396
00:33:32,045 --> 00:33:32,726
[SPEAKER_01]: But I won't say that.

397
00:33:33,406 --> 00:33:35,248
[SPEAKER_01]: I will not deliberately accept it.

398
00:33:37,650 --> 00:33:41,253
[SPEAKER_01]: But what if it stays there for like six months, pressuring me?

399
00:33:41,513 --> 00:33:44,895
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter if it stays for 60 months, 60 years, six eons.

400
00:33:46,377 --> 00:33:47,137
[SPEAKER_01]: I won't say it.

401
00:33:47,257 --> 00:33:49,179
[SPEAKER_01]: I won't accept that to be...

402
00:33:49,359 --> 00:33:50,360
[SPEAKER_01]: I won't accept that act.

403
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:51,581
[SPEAKER_01]: I won't accept those images.

404
00:33:52,563 --> 00:33:53,924
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's usually why people give in.

405
00:33:54,265 --> 00:33:55,406
[SPEAKER_01]: What if this lasts forever?

406
00:33:55,426 --> 00:33:56,527
[SPEAKER_01]: It's like, well, that's the training.

407
00:33:58,929 --> 00:34:01,631
[SPEAKER_01]: Pressuring images, they want you to accept them.

408
00:34:03,953 --> 00:34:08,657
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you don't accept them, they're going to obviously pressure you more to accept them.

409
00:34:08,677 --> 00:34:13,041
[SPEAKER_01]: But they can't do anything else to you, except trying to pressure you into accepting them.

410
00:34:14,142 --> 00:34:18,927
[SPEAKER_01]: So, as you might feel like scared and overwhelming initially, but you know, well, that is the root of the problem.

411
00:34:19,792 --> 00:34:31,996
[SPEAKER_01]: Everything else that follows, all this... all the things that I've previously restrained, all the unwholesome, was all just the result of this accepting images of the unwholesome nature, deliberately allowing them to take the center stage.

412
00:34:33,556 --> 00:34:37,837
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if I never do that, I don't have to worry about anything else at all.

413
00:34:38,378 --> 00:34:39,358
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if those images...

414
00:34:40,257 --> 00:34:47,279
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if they keep coming, as I said, for next 60 years, you realize, well, not accepting them, it's kind of effortless.

415
00:34:47,579 --> 00:34:50,100
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't need to go anywhere, climb the mountains.

416
00:34:51,360 --> 00:34:52,221
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't need to do anything.

417
00:34:52,801 --> 00:34:54,701
[SPEAKER_01]: Accept mentally.

418
00:34:54,861 --> 00:34:57,782
[SPEAKER_01]: Not accept them deliberately and allow them to take the center stage.

419
00:34:57,822 --> 00:34:58,842
[SPEAKER_01]: That's all I need to do.

420
00:34:59,983 --> 00:35:00,903
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it is peaceful.

421
00:35:00,963 --> 00:35:01,623
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not a fight.

422
00:35:01,643 --> 00:35:02,043
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not a...

423
00:35:02,123 --> 00:35:02,704
[SPEAKER_03]: It's... exactly.

424
00:35:02,924 --> 00:35:03,184
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

425
00:35:04,124 --> 00:35:04,584
[SPEAKER_02]: A task.

426
00:35:04,964 --> 00:35:07,585
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize why it would result in the equanimity, completely.

427
00:35:09,007 --> 00:35:12,872
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, there will be no room for ill will, nor any room for sensuality.

428
00:35:18,599 --> 00:35:21,143
[SPEAKER_00]: I was gonna say, like, you realize that kind of...

429
00:35:22,273 --> 00:35:29,759
[SPEAKER_00]: Fearing, what if this pressure keeps pressuring me for whatever... That's actually, that's the, that's why it's pressuring.

430
00:35:29,819 --> 00:35:29,999
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

431
00:35:30,119 --> 00:35:33,061
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not, it's not, it's not it that is pressuring you.

432
00:35:33,462 --> 00:35:46,431
[SPEAKER_00]: If you kind of stop fearing it pressuring you, and you just say, well, yeah, you can keep for however long it takes, infinite, infinitely, like infinite, infinitely patient, I suppose, in regards.

433
00:35:46,451 --> 00:35:46,972
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

434
00:35:47,332 --> 00:35:47,792
[SPEAKER_00]: It cannot

435
00:35:48,973 --> 00:35:50,754
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no room for any pressure there.

436
00:35:51,274 --> 00:35:57,478
[SPEAKER_00]: Because if you're infinitely patient, there's... that's almost like the definition of just something that's not bothering you at all.

437
00:35:57,518 --> 00:35:58,098
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the point.

438
00:35:58,218 --> 00:36:00,780
[SPEAKER_01]: Developing patience in regard to the right things.

439
00:36:01,060 --> 00:36:09,104
[SPEAKER_01]: People can develop patience in regard to things that do not necessarily... that still imply the wrong view, that still imply that the problem is in the wrong place.

440
00:36:10,205 --> 00:36:14,307
[SPEAKER_01]: But when it comes to this true restraint, true physical restraint, verbal restraint,

441
00:36:15,423 --> 00:36:20,567
[SPEAKER_01]: Once you recognize the deliberate acceptance of unwholesome thoughts on the mental level, it's okay.

442
00:36:20,587 --> 00:36:27,252
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if I develop patience in regard to that, then, yeah, that's pretty much the root of the development.

443
00:36:37,598 --> 00:36:40,703
[SPEAKER_01]: And that is like the the true kind of patient endurance.

444
00:36:40,783 --> 00:36:52,841
[SPEAKER_01]: Obviously, patient endurance has to be exercised in regard to the body when you're pressured to act, in regard to the verbal when you're pressured to act, but the root of it is patient endurance in regard to the images associated with unwholesome,

445
00:36:53,402 --> 00:36:55,383
[SPEAKER_01]: They want me to accept them.

446
00:36:55,523 --> 00:36:59,764
[SPEAKER_01]: They want me to deliberately allow them, welcome them, to take the center stage.

447
00:36:59,884 --> 00:37:07,026
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, even if I then practice mindfulness and read the suttas and do all of this, all of that I do in response.

448
00:37:07,187 --> 00:37:13,048
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that I do as a way of managing the fact that I couldn't help but welcome them and open the door for them.

449
00:37:14,209 --> 00:37:14,389
[SPEAKER_01]: So,

450
00:37:15,222 --> 00:37:18,684
[SPEAKER_01]: Not welcoming them does not equal denying them.

451
00:37:19,324 --> 00:37:21,165
[SPEAKER_01]: It simply equals not welcoming them.

452
00:37:21,845 --> 00:37:25,527
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if they remain sitting in your face for as long as they want.

453
00:37:25,547 --> 00:37:26,308
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the practice.

454
00:37:27,548 --> 00:37:35,372
[SPEAKER_01]: Learning how to sustain that yoniso manasikāra, the right way of attending to them, as if you are not welcome, regardless of everything else.

455
00:37:37,854 --> 00:37:38,754
[SPEAKER_01]: And then they'll stop coming.

456
00:37:39,595 --> 00:37:39,995
[SPEAKER_01]: Completely.

457
00:37:45,877 --> 00:37:47,838
[SPEAKER_01]: And you realize, yeah, you truly obliterated them.

458
00:37:49,879 --> 00:37:50,439
[SPEAKER_01]: Destroyed them.

459
00:37:50,779 --> 00:37:51,379
[SPEAKER_01]: Surpassed them.

460
00:37:53,520 --> 00:37:54,961
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, they're not coming up anymore.

461
00:37:55,161 --> 00:37:55,581
[SPEAKER_01]: Factually.

462
00:37:55,941 --> 00:37:56,501
[SPEAKER_01]: They're gone.

463
00:37:56,521 --> 00:38:09,487
[SPEAKER_03]: Would you say this is the... the definition... the difference between... it's a mind or the definition in the suttas that you read about quite often, limited and unlimited.

464
00:38:10,307 --> 00:38:11,928
[SPEAKER_03]: So, your mind is limited by this...

465
00:38:12,870 --> 00:38:13,310
[SPEAKER_03]: Ill-will.

466
00:38:13,871 --> 00:38:16,972
[SPEAKER_03]: And now, it is not limited by that thing.

467
00:38:17,472 --> 00:38:18,673
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not bound to it.

468
00:38:19,373 --> 00:38:20,414
[SPEAKER_01]: And, well, yes, yes.

469
00:38:20,514 --> 00:38:23,976
[SPEAKER_01]: There would be, there would be like a different degrees of limit as well.

470
00:38:24,696 --> 00:38:41,005
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, see, once this, once this becomes more and more apparent, through being rightly restrained, rightly established in your precepts, in your speech, then you start to recognize that the deliberate welcoming of thoughts, obviously, you know,

471
00:38:42,108 --> 00:38:43,970
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said, it's not going to be perfect overnight.

472
00:38:44,050 --> 00:38:46,953
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you might not do it, but then you might do a little bit.

473
00:38:47,833 --> 00:38:54,760
[SPEAKER_01]: So, to the extent that you allow it, to take the center stage, to the center you welcome it, to that extent you're limited.

474
00:38:55,040 --> 00:39:01,967
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you might be less limited than before, but if there is the slightest extent of welcoming such thoughts,

475
00:39:02,838 --> 00:39:04,159
[SPEAKER_01]: So, to that extent, there is a limit.

476
00:39:04,739 --> 00:39:11,722
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when you truly, then, mind is completely free from slightest degree of welcoming those thoughts, your mind is unlimited.

477
00:39:11,742 --> 00:39:17,585
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's basically when you are surmounted the five hindrances.

478
00:39:18,485 --> 00:39:20,466
[SPEAKER_03]: So, the ill will is not limiting you.

479
00:39:22,547 --> 00:39:26,548
[SPEAKER_01]: You deliberately allowing it to take the center stage is the limit.

480
00:39:27,269 --> 00:39:28,289
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what limits it.

481
00:39:28,569 --> 00:39:29,590
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what narrows it down.

